                {
                  "id": "c71f3009-a3f4-4aa5-aaf0-d0f667100e56",
                  "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
                  "name": "Help",
                  "label": "📖 Help",
                  "type": 10,
                  "description": "Show workbook help or change log information",
                  "isRequired": true,
                  "typeSettings": {
                    "additionalResourceOptions": [],
                    "showDefault": false
                  },
                  "jsonData": "[\r\n  { \"value\": \"Yes\", \"label\": \"Yes\" },\r\n  { \"value\": \"No\", \"label\": \"No\", \"selected\": true },\r\n  { \"value\": \"Change Log\", \"label\": \"Change Log\" }\r\n]"
                }
              ],
              "style": "above",
              "queryType": 1,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.resourcegraph/resources"
            },
            "customWidth": "75",
            "name": "parameters - 1"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "# Change Log\n\n| Version                      | Changes                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **v1.2 — 26 September 2026** | Added a dedicated **🌱 Sanctioned AI Agents** selector for local agents, cloud agents, local model hosts and agentic tools.                                                 |\n|                              | Added the separate **AIAgentGovernance** Sentinel watchlist and `ai_agent_governance_watchlist.csv` upload file, using `Key` as the SearchKey column.                       |\n|                              | Added automatic selection of agent watchlist rows marked `Sanctioned=TRUE`, while preserving manual selection from the public catalogue.                                    |\n|                              | Added Local and Cloud **AI Agent Governance at a Glance** summaries for sanctioned observed, unsanctioned observed and sanctioned not observed activity.                    |\n|                              | Added Local and Cloud **Sanctioned Agents Not Observed** reports for selected agents with no evidence during the selected Time Range.                                       |\n|                              | Added optional-table handling for Cloud agent telemetry so unavailable audit sources do not prevent the report from running.                                                |\n|                              | Normalised agent keys and consolidated results to one row per tool or agent to prevent duplicate report rows.                                                               |\n|                              | Clarified the separation between the public detection catalogue, governance watchlists and risk classification.                                                             |\n| **v1.1 — 22 September 2026** | Refined AI governance mapping around stable **PolicyKey** identifiers, supporting both domain-based services and process-only AI tools.                                     |\n|                              | Added optional **AIGovernance** watchlist support for customer-specific AI products, local catalogue overrides and automatic selection of entries marked `Sanctioned=TRUE`. |\n|                              | Added **AI Usage & Adoption**, including active days, observed sessions, users, devices and activity volume across the selected Time Range.                                 |\n|                              | Added **AI Usage by User**, providing per-user activity patterns, product usage, observed sessions and supporting telemetry.                                                |\n|                              | Clarified the separation between **governance status** and **risk classification** for AI agents and tools.                                                                 |\n|                              | Expanded workbook guidance for catalogue configuration, telemetry interpretation and inferred usage measures.                                                               |\n| **v1.0**                     | Initial public preview of the **AI Governance** workbook.                                                                                                                   |\n|                              | Added configurable **Sanctioned AI Services** policy selection.                                                                                                             |\n|                              | Added 🟢 **Sanctioned**, 🔴 **Unsanctioned**, and 🟠 **Mixed** governance classification.                                                                                   |\n|                              | Added consolidated **AI Compliance & Governance Review** covering browser, API/developer, non-browser network and desktop-client activity.                                  |\n|                              | Added compact **Sanctioned and Unsanctioned AI Product** summaries based on distinct observed users.                                                                        |\n|                              | Added **New AI Users** using a fixed 30-day observation window to identify users first observed during the most recent 7 days.                                              |\n|                              | Added **Multi-AI Product Usage** across web and desktop-client activity.                                                                                                    |\n|                              | Added **AI Agent / Tool Detection** using a public AI agent watchlist, including governance mapping and separate risk classification.                                       |\n|                              | Added support for the workbook **Time Range** across applicable activity reports.                                                                                           |\n|                              | Designed as a lightweight, publicly shareable AI governance workbook using Microsoft Defender telemetry.                                                                    |\n"
            },
            "customWidth": "50",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Help",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "Change Log"
            },
            "name": "text - 7"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "# 🤖 AI Governance\n\nThis workbook provides a high-level view of **AI usage and agent activity observed through Microsoft Defender telemetry**, helping organisations understand which AI services, local agents and cloud agents are being used and whether that activity aligns with approved policy.\n\n## 🟢 Sanctioned AI Services\n\nUse the **Sanctioned AI Services** selector to choose the AI products approved for use within your organisation.\n\nThe service catalogue uses stable **PolicyKey** identifiers so governance can be applied consistently to web services, network activity, desktop clients and process-only AI tools.\n\nAn optional Sentinel watchlist with alias **AIGovernance** can add customer-specific AI products, override matching public catalogue entries and automatically select local entries marked `Sanctioned=TRUE`. Local catalogue entries are shown with **[Local]**. The public catalogue remains available when the watchlist is absent.\n\n## 🤖 Sanctioned AI Agents and Tools\n\nUse the **🌱 Sanctioned AI Agents** selector to choose the AI agents, local model hosts and agentic tools approved for use within your organisation.\n\nThe public `ai_agent_watchlist.csv` catalogue is used to match local and cloud agents. An optional local governance file, `ai_agent_governance_watchlist.csv`, can be uploaded to Sentinel as the **AIAgentGovernance** watchlist. Select **Key** as the SearchKey column. Rows marked `Sanctioned=TRUE` are selected automatically and local entries are shown with **[Local]**.\n\nThe AI agent governance watchlist is separate from the AI services governance watchlist. If **AIAgentGovernance** is absent, the public agent catalogue and manual selector continue to work.\n\nAgent activity is classified as:\n\n* 🟢 **Sanctioned** — activity associated with a selected approved agent or tool.\n* 🔴 **Unsanctioned** — recognised agent or tool activity not included in the selected policy.\n* ⚪ **Sanctioned not observed** — a selected sanctioned agent with no matching evidence during the selected **Time Range**.\n\nIf no agents are selected, all recognised AI agent and tool activity is treated as **unsanctioned**.\n\n## 📊 Reports\n\n**AI Compliance & Governance Review** provides the main view of sanctioned and unsanctioned AI service activity, including browser, API/developer, non-browser network and desktop-client evidence.\n\n**Local AI Agent Governance at a Glance** summarises sanctioned agents observed, unsanctioned agents observed and selected sanctioned agents with no local process evidence during the selected **Time Range**.\n\n**Cloud AI Agent Governance at a Glance** provides the equivalent summary for cloud audit and identity telemetry.\n\n**Local and Cloud Sanctioned Agents Not Observed** list selected sanctioned agents for which no evidence was found in the applicable telemetry during the selected **Time Range**.\n\n**Local AI Agent / Tool Detection** identifies agents, local model hosts and agentic tooling executing on endpoints. **Cloud AI Agent / Tool Detection** identifies recognised cloud agents through available audit and identity telemetry. Results are grouped into one row per detected agent.\n\n## 🛡️ Interpreting the Results\n\nNetwork, process, audit and identity telemetry demonstrates observed communication, execution or service activity. It does **not** establish user intent, the content submitted to an AI service or agent, or the amount of time a user actively spent using it.\n\nRisk and recommended action values come from the detection catalogue and are separate from sanctioned or unsanctioned governance status.\n\n## 🛡️ Microsoft Defender Data Requirements\n\nThe workbook primarily uses:\n\n* `DeviceNetworkEvents` — observed connections to recognised AI services.\n* `DeviceProcessEvents` — execution of recognised AI clients, agents, model hosts and related processes.\n* `OfficeActivity` — Microsoft 365 and Purview audit activity.\n* `AuditLogs` — Microsoft Entra audit activity.\n* `AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs` — Microsoft Entra service-principal sign-in activity.\n* The optional **AIGovernance** and **AIAgentGovernance** watchlists — customer-specific catalogue entries and sanctioned-policy defaults.\n\nCloud sources are queried opportunistically; unavailable tables are ignored. Results depend on Microsoft Defender licensing, endpoint onboarding, available telemetry and retention.\n\n> **Tip:** Where the required Defender telemetry is not available through Microsoft Sentinel, try the workbook from **Microsoft Defender → Microsoft Sentinel → Workbooks**.\n"
            },
            "customWidth": "50",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "Help",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "Yes"
            },
            "name": "text - 7 - Copy"
          }
        ],
        "exportParameters": true
      },
      "name": "group - parameter and help"
    },
    {
      "type": 11,
      "content": {
        "version": "LinkItem/1.0",
        "style": "tabs",
        "links": [
          {
            "id": "e3821f6a-8198-4e0b-a31c-0b16f6b2436f",
            "cellValue": "selectedTab",
